course: dictionary
lesson: 552
title: Attitude: how you think and feel
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An attitude is the way you think and feel about something, and it often shows in how you behave. A teacher might praise your good attitude to learning when you try hard and do not give up.
explain: Use the words around it to work out the meaning. «Coaches notice attitude, and cheering and watching the game keep a sub ready to go on.» Cheering and watching show that attitude is about how the players think, feel and act during a game. Try it: swap in "way of thinking" and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: An attitude can be good or bad. A positive attitude is hopeful and keen, while a bad attitude is the opposite. In another example, old fears about food were partly mixed with «unfair attitudes» to Chinese food, which means people had unfair feelings about it.
fact: Attitude means the way you think and feel about something, and how that shows in what you do.
fact: «Attitude» on its own can mean rude behaviour, as in «Don't give me attitude.» This is an informal use.
fact: Attitude can also mean the position of your body, as in «He stood in a relaxed attitude.»
fact: Useful phrases are «a positive attitude», «a bad attitude», «change your attitude» and «attitude towards».
fact: In a story, a character's attitude can change as they learn a lesson.
exercise: «Coaches notice attitude, and cheering and watching the game keep a sub ready to go on.» What does attitude mean here? | Shoes and kit worn by the players | *The way the players think, feel and act | The final score of the game | The number on a shirt
exercise: Dad says, «Don't give me attitude.» What does attitude mean here? | *Being rude or not caring about others | Feeling sleepy after dinner | A long way to travel | Being very kind and helpful
exercise: A teacher says, «You have a positive attitude to learning.» What does positive attitude mean? | Lazy and bored with lessons | Tired from sleeping late | *Hopeful, keen and trying hard | Loud and noisy in class
test: «He stood in a relaxed attitude, leaning against the wall.» What does attitude mean here? | *The way his body was positioned | A rude remark | A long holiday | A school subject
test: In a story, the hero's attitude changes after she learns a lesson. What does this tell you? | Her clothes have changed | She has forgotten her name | *The way she thinks and feels is now different | She has moved house
exam: Which phrase means a hopeful, keen way of thinking? | a long walk | *a positive attitude | a rude remark | a loud whisper
